  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q28-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "28",
    "prompt": "In the ghastly game of Russian Roulette, a player places a single bullet in a six-shot revolver, spins the cylinder, places the muzzle against their head, and pulls the trigger.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q28-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the probability that a player survives two consecutive trigger pulls in a single turn, assuming the player re-spins the cylinder before each pull.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{25}{36}$",
          "worked": "Each pull has survival probability $\\frac56$. Re-spinning makes the pulls independent.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{survives both pulls})&=\\frac56\\times\\frac56\\\\P(\\text{survives both pulls})&=\\frac{25}{36}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q28-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the probability that a player survives $n$ consecutive trigger pulls in a single turn, assuming the player re-spins the cylinder before each pull.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(\\dfrac56\\right)^n$",
          "worked": "The $n$ pulls are independent, each with survival probability $\\frac56$.\n\n$$P(\\text{survives all }n\\text{ pulls})=\\left(\\frac56\\right)^n.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q28-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Consider a variation with two players taking turns pulling the trigger (re-spinning before each turn) until someone is shot. Find the probability that the first player gets shot.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac6{11}$\n\nLet $p$ be the required probability. The reset equation is $p=\\frac16+\\left(\\frac56\\right)^2p$.",
          "worked": "Let $p$ be the probability that the first player is shot. Either this happens on the first turn, or both players survive and the situation resets.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}p&=\\frac16+\\left(\\frac56\\right)^2p\\\\p&=\\frac16+\\frac{25}{36}p\\\\36p&=6+25p\\\\11p&=6\\\\p&=\\frac6{11}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p26-q28-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Now suppose $n$ players take turns with a $k$-shot revolver containing one bullet, re-spinning before each turn. Find the probability that the first player is shot, in terms of $n$ and $k$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{k^{n-1}}{k^n-(k-1)^n}$\n\nUse $p=\\frac1k+\\left(\\frac{k-1}{k}\\right)^np$: after all $n$ players survive, the situation resets.",
          "worked": "Let $p$ be the probability that the first player is shot. The probability of being shot on a turn is $\\frac1k$. If all $n$ players survive, the situation resets.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}p&=\\frac1k+\\left(\\frac{k-1}{k}\\right)^np\\\\p\\left[1-\\left(\\frac{k-1}{k}\\right)^n\\right]&=\\frac1k\\\\p&=\\frac{1/k}{1-(k-1)^n/k^n}\\\\p&=\\frac{k^{n-1}}{k^n-(k-1)^n}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      }
    ]
  },
